{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3n8mBaF5ksVxvKZDu5H","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the misspelling and committed it as a single commit, `9cec18f`. \"wholsale\" appeared once each in `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv`, and nowhere else. `scripts/check.sh` passed before the commit. To undo it in one step, run `git revert 9cec18f`.\n\n**The commit message needs your call.** CLAUDE.md says commit messages start with the data month because the import log groups commits by that prefix. This fix covers three months, so I used `2025-10..2025-12: fix category typo wholsale -> wholesale`. If the import log reads the prefix strictly, it might not file that under any month. Your options:\n- **Keep the range prefix**, if the log handles it.\n- **Use one month**, such as `2025-12:`, by amending the message. It stays one commit.\n- **Split into three commits**, one per month. The grouping is cleaner, but undoing it takes three reverts, which goes against what you asked for.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":331,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":21510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-68>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:37:28.510Z","request_id":"gen-1794703044-hFjebas7jYsUkxLFb2rc"}
